        "providerType": "Competence centre",
        "providerCountry": "Italy",
        "providerCity": "Trento",
        "providerDescription": "TrentinoSalute4.0 is a local digital health competence centre that unites the Autonomous Province of Trento (PAT), the Provincial Healthcare Trust (APSS), and the Bruno Kessler Foundation (FBK).",
        "outcomes": [
            "STEMlab"
        ],
        "challenges": [
            "DI"
        ],
        "challengeDescription": "DI - Digitalization and Innovation | Initial situation: Growing need for more efficient management of chronic disease, particularly Type 2 diabetes, in the face of increasing patient numbers and healthcare resource constraints. | Challenge faced: Ensuring accessibility and reliable use of telemedicine tools, Technological reliability, User engagement, and Digital Literacy.",
        "mainResultsSummary": "In Trentino, the solution was planned by first analyzing current healthcare models and identifying the potential to improve efficiency and quality of care through digitalization. The project involved the use of the TreC Diabete platform (developed by TrentinoSalute4.0), which was integrated into the care protocols of diabetes centers in Trentino. Patients were enrolled in the study, and data were regularly collected through the app. Healthcare providers could monitor this data and provide feedback, reducing the need for in-person visits. | Main results Summary: | Clinical outcomes: Patients using the app showed comparable results to the control group in terms of blood glucose levels, though there was a noticeable reduction in HbA1c in patients participating in the study (a key marker for diabetes control), | Direct communication between patients and healthcare professionals through the app, | Monitoring and alerts to the healthcare professionals, enabling timely interventions without the need for frequent in-person visits, | User-friendly app, accessible for people with varying levels of digital literacy. | Potential transferability to further organisations: Several aspects can be replicated, including the integration of telemedicine solutions like the TreC Diabete app for remote monitoring and communication and the cross-regional collaboration across Trentino, Lombardy, and Tuscany healthcare ecosystems.",
        "scope": "Cross-regional (Trentino, Lombardy and Tuscany)",
        "language": "Italian, English",
        "thirdParties": "TrentinoSalute4.0",
