        "challengeDescription": "DI - Digitalization and Innovation | Initial situation: European industrial sectors, particularly SMEs, often lacked resources and connections to integrate advanced technologies into their processes and value chains. | Challenge faced: Uptake of advanced and digital technologies across regions and industries, overcoming fragmentation of innovation ecosystems. | EFS - Economic Sustainability and Policy Challenges | Initial situation: There was a lack of aligned and accessible funding mechanisms to support cross-regional innovation and scaling-up. | Challenge faced: Developing a sustainable interregional funding mechanism that can bridge regional, national, and EU-level investment strategies.",
        "mainResultsSummary": "The Vanguard Initiative promotes interregional pilot projects that connect clusters, businesses, and research institutions around shared smart specialisation strategies. Additionally, it advocates for stronger synergies between EU, regional, and national funding to support innovation and technology uptake. The initiative also provides financial support for interregional innovation to stakeholders, including SMEs and research institutions, through calls for proposals. | Main results Summary: | Enhanced interregional collaboration between European advanced industrial regions; | Acceleration of innovation and technology uptake through pilot projects; | Reduction of regional innovation gaps; | Stronger multi-level governance. | Potential transferability to further organisations: the place-based, multi-level collaboration and funding model can be transferred to other sectors, including the health and care ecosystems.",
