        "receiverDescription": "The Landeskrankenhaus Villach is one of the largest hospitals in Carinthia, Austria, and part of the public hospital association KABEG. It provides comprehensive medical and surgical care, and has recently positioned itself as a pioneer in sustainable and climate-conscious healthcare by implementing green innovations across clinical operations.",
        "providerOrganization": "KABEG – Landeskrankenhaus Villach (internes Green Team)",
        "providerType": "Public Hospital",
        "providerCountry": "Austria",
        "providerCity": "Villach",
        "providerDescription": "KABEG LKH Villach itself acts as both the initiator and implementer of the climate-awareness project. The interdisciplinary Green Team, consisting of medical staff, facility managers, and sustainability experts, develops and pilots climate-friendly processes in real clinical settings (e.g. energy, mobility, waste, anesthetic gas recycling). The team also works on staff and patient engagement and functions as an internal innovation driver.",
