        "challengeDescription": "Initial situation: | Aging population in Lucerne with limited mechanisms for structured engagement of older citizens in policy-making and city development. | Challenge faced: | Growing need for inclusive aging strategies that enable participation, prevent social isolation, and tap into the skills of older adults.",
        "mainResultsSummary": "How the solution was planned and implemented:\n Luzern60plus was initiated by the City of Lucerne as a participatory platform to develop resource-based aging strategies. The platform facilitates structured dialogue, publishes reports and motions, and organizes events and thematic working groups. | Tangible results: | Regular motions to the City Council from seniors’ working groups | City-issued reports and evaluations on aging topics | A participatory governance structure that connects civil society and policymakers | Raised awareness and political momentum around aging | Transferability:\n The concept can be adapted in other cities and regions seeking to institutionalize participatory aging policy. Its low-threshold, dialogue-based format is scalable and relevant across various Alpine Space contexts. | https://www.luzern60plus.ch/altern-luzern/berichte-und-antraege-des-grossen-stadtrates",
