        "challengeDescription": "Initial situation | Patients and caregivers often create innovative solutions to manage their specific health challenges. These inventions typically remain undocumented and inaccessible to others facing similar problems.",
        "mainResultsSummary": "How the solution was planned and implemented | Patient Innovation was initiated through academic research and transformed into a live digital platform. The team built partnerships with universities, hospitals, and NGOs to identify and promote solutions. All contributions are reviewed by a medical team before being published. It evolved into a global open innovation community. | Consequences and tangible results | Over 1,000 health-related solutions published | Engaged innovators from more than 80 countries | Empowered patients and caregivers to co-create the future of care | Featured in academic publications, conferences, and international media | Potential transferability to further organisations | Very high. The platform is open, multilingual, and scalable. It offers inspiration and concrete ideas for hospitals, design labs, makerspaces, and digital health ecosystems in the Alpine region and beyond.",
