        "challengeDescription": "Initial situation | Swiss hospitals face increasing demands for high-quality, efficient, patient-centered services. At the same time, fragmented digital ecosystems, complex governance, and siloed infrastructures limit their ability to innovate systemically.",
        "mainResultsSummary": "How the solution was planned and implemented | SHIFT was launched in 2022 as part of Innosuisse’s Flagship Programme to tackle systemic healthcare transformation. A cross-sectoral consortium defined a multi-year work plan involving co-creation workshops, technology development, hospital piloting, and policy engagement. Hospitals act as real-life labs to test and refine digital tools and frameworks. | Consequences and tangible results | Development of a blueprint for smart & liquid hospitals | New models for AI integration, data governance, and care coordination | Launch of a shared knowledge platform to disseminate results | Cross-sector partnerships between hospitals, tech providers, and academia | Strategic groundwork for long-term healthcare transformation in Switzerland | Potential transferability to further organisations | High. The modular design of SHIFT enables adaptation in other health systems. The tools, governance frameworks, and policy recommendations emerging from the project are suitable for Alpine partners seeking digital transformation roadmaps or smart hospital strategies.",
