        "mainResultsSummary": "How the solution was planned and then implemented | Vicino Luzern was founded as a community-led response to aging challenges. Through a multistakeholder model involving healthcare providers, municipalities, and civil society, the initiative implemented a neighborhood-focused coordination structure. A hub was created to provide advice, organize services, connect residents, and identify emerging needs. | Consequences and tangible results | Significant increase in early identification and support of vulnerable seniors | Coordination model that eases the burden on formal care actors | Strong user satisfaction and engagement in community-based events | Integration of Vicino within local care planning processes | Annual reports provide insights for municipal and cantonal partners | Potential transferability to further organisations | Very high. The Vicino model is scalable for small towns and cities alike, offering a flexible, participatory structure adaptable to different legal and financial fra??",
